  "details": "<p>The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: Castleford</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "Roman Lagentium (modern Castleford) is the site of a series of forts, beginning with a Flavian fort that was later replaced by a second-century fort. The site of the fort was occupied from ca. A.D. 80 to 150 while the vicus remained occupied until the fourth century.",
